        "raw": "<p>That&#39;s easy.</p><p>Kaargra plays Get Back In There and Bloodsworn Judgement. &nbsp;This puts Kaargra in play, and attaches Chaos Lord to her.</p><p>Now, every time Kaargra is dealt damage, she plays the top card of her deck. &nbsp;This means that by the fifth turn, Kaargra could have as many as 5 gladiators and herself in play, with an option on one more. &nbsp;Legacy Galvanizes, and on the fifth turn, Unity Hastily Augments O-X&#39;s Defensive Blast, to deal 4 damage 4 times to 6 targets. &nbsp;That&#39;s 16 damage, and more than enough favor to guarentee the victory, assuming that you also kill Kaargra.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>To kill Kaargra at this point, you need to have done 24 damage to her already. &nbsp;Legacy uses Galavanize and Inspiring Presence. &nbsp;Chronoranger plays Eye On the Prize x3, Displaced Armory for his Hat, Displaced Armory for Compounded Bow. &nbsp;7x3 = 21 damage. &nbsp;Then Ra plays Fire Blast.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And that&#39;s without pulling in the Scholar for chained Don&#39;t Dismiss Anythings.</p>",
